#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:99
msgid "Exercise 1: analysis of a nucleation trajectory I"
msgstr "演習1：Nucleation Trajectory の解析 I"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:103
msgid ""
"We can start by using plumed to analyze a trajectory and identify the total "
"number of atoms belonging to a liquid phase condensing from a supersaturated"
" vapour in a long unbiased MD simulation."
msgstr ""
"まず、長い Unbiased MD シミュレーションの Trajectory を PLUMED で解析し、過飽和蒸気から Condensation "
"する液相に属する原子の総数を求める。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:107
msgid ""
"To this aim, a typical choice is the implementation of a criterion inspired "
"by the work of Ten Wolde and Frenkel: all the atoms with a threshold number "
"of nearest neighbours larger than a threshold is considered as part of the "
"liquid phase."
msgstr ""
"このためには、Ten Wolde と Frenkel の研究に着想を得た判定基準を用いるのが一般的である。Nearest Neighbours "
"の数が所定の閾値を超える原子を、すべて液相に属するとみなす。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:111
msgid ""
"In PLUMED this criterion can be readily implemented using the multicolvar "
"[COORDINATIONNUMBER](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/_c_o_o_r_d_i_n_a_t_i_o_n_n_u_m_b_e_r.html):"
msgstr ""
"PLUMED では、multicolvar の [COORDINATIONNUMBER](https://www.plumed.org/doc-"
"master/user-doc/html/_c_o_o_r_d_i_n_a_t_i_o_n_n_u_m_b_e_r.html) "
"を用いて、この基準を容易に実装できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:127
msgid ""
"The time evolution of the number of atoms in the liquid phase can be "
"computed by analyzing the trajectory using the "
"[driver](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/driver.html) "
"functionality (where liquid.dat is the plumed file for this analysis)."
msgstr ""
"液相中の原子数の時間変化は、[driver](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/driver.html) 機能で Trajectory を解析して計算できる。ここで liquid.dat は、この解析用の "
"PLUMED ファイルである。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:139 INSTRUCTIONS.md:217 INSTRUCTIONS.md:307
#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:397
msgid "Try on your own"
msgstr "自分で試す"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:143
msgid ""
"Using other MultiColvar keywords can you count the number of atoms on the "
"surface of the clusters forming in this trajectory? Can you estimate how the"
" surface to volume ratio of the droplets forming in the system changes "
"directly within PLUMED?"
msgstr ""
"他の MultiColvar キーワードを用いて、この Trajectory で形成される Clusters "
"の表面にある原子の数を数えられるだろうか。系内にできる Droplets の Surface-to-Volume Ratio の変化を、PLUMED "
"内で直接推定できるだろうか。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:147 INSTRUCTIONS.md:225 INSTRUCTIONS.md:317
#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:381
msgid "Available data"
msgstr "利用できるデータ"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:151 INSTRUCTIONS.md:229
msgid ""
"The MD trajectory that we will analyze can be found in the folder called "
"`data`:"
msgstr "解析する MD Trajectory は `data` フォルダにある。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:153 INSTRUCTIONS.md:231
msgid ""
"`LJvap.gro`: reference conformation of 10000 LJ particles in a metastable "
"vapour phase."
msgstr ""
"`LJvap.gro`：Metastable Vapour Phase にある10000個の LJ Particles の Reference "
"Conformation。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:155 INSTRUCTIONS.md:233
msgid "`LJvap_to_liq.xtc`: trajectory."
msgstr "`LJvap_to_liq.xtc`：Trajectory。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:159
msgid "Exercise 2: analysis of a nucleation trajectory II"
msgstr "演習2：Nucleation Trajectory の解析 II"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:163
msgid ""
"In certain contexts, it can be helpful to characterize the phase transition "
"by following analyzing the population of clusters that form during the "
"nucleation process. In PLUMED, this is possible by taking advantage of the "
"[DFSCLUSTERING](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/_d_f_s_c_l_u_s_t_e_r_i_n_g.html) algorithm, which builds on the "
"construction of a [CONTACT_MATRIX](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/_c_o_n_t_a_c_t__m_a_t_r_i_x.html) to identify clusters of atoms "
"with specific properties."
msgstr ""
"状況によっては、Nucleation の過程で形成される Clusters の Population を解析し、Phase Transition "
"を特徴付けると有用である。PLUMED では、[CONTACT_MATRIX](https://www.plumed.org/doc-"
"master/user-doc/html/_c_o_n_t_a_c_t__m_a_t_r_i_x.html) の構築に基づいて、特定の性質を持つ原子の "
"Clusters を識別する [DFSCLUSTERING](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/_d_f_s_c_l_u_s_t_e_r_i_n_g.html) アルゴリズムを利用できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:167
msgid ""
"Here we analyse the clusters distribution emerging in the trajectory "
"`LJvap_to_liq.xtc`, focussing on the number of clusters, and following the "
"evolution of the four largest clusters in the system:"
msgstr ""
"ここでは、Trajectory `LJvap_to_liq.xtc` に現れる Cluster Distribution を解析する。Clusters "
"の数に注目し、系内で最大の4つの Clusters の時間変化を追う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:221
msgid ""
"Modifying the setup above, can you compute the number of clusters with a "
"size larger than 20 LJ particles?"
msgstr "上の設定を変更して、20個を超える LJ Particles からなる Clusters の数を計算できるだろうか。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:237
msgid "Exercise 3: Steady-state diffusive flux with CmuMD"
msgstr "演習3：CmuMD による Steady-state Diffusive Flux"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:241
msgid ""
"In the two examples discussed in Exercises 1 and 2 it is apparent that the "
"process of condensation reaches steady state due to finite-size effects. "
"However, looking at the process more carefully, one can notice that the "
"driving force leading to phase separation is far from constant."
msgstr ""
"演習1と2の例では、Finite-size Effects によって Condensation が Steady State "
"に達することが分かる。しかし過程を詳しく見ると、Phase Separation の Driving Force は一定とは大きく異なる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:243
msgid ""
"C$\\mu$MD allows using PLUMED to apply ad-hoc forces and keep constant the "
"composition of spatial regions of the simulation box called control regions."
" This feature allows to model processes driven by concentration in steady, "
"out-of-equilibrium conditions."
msgstr ""
"C$\\mu$MD では、PLUMED を使って目的に応じた Force を加え、Simulation Box 内の Control Regions "
"と呼ばれる空間領域の組成を一定に保てる。この機能により、濃度を Driving Force とする過程を、定常的な非平衡条件でモデル化できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:247
msgid ""
"The first example we will focus on is a purely diffusive process in a LJ "
"vapour."
msgstr "最初に扱う例は、LJ Vapour 中の純粋な Diffusion 過程である。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:251
msgid ""
"A PLUMED file that allows imposing a steady concentration difference with "
"CmuMD looks like:"
msgstr "CmuMD で一定の濃度差を与える PLUMED ファイルは、次のようになる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:295
msgid "We can run a CMUMD simulation under these conditions as:"
msgstr "この条件での CMUMD シミュレーションは、次のように実行できる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:311
msgid "Perform simulations at varying concentration differences."
msgstr "濃度差を変えながらシミュレーションを実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:313
msgid ""
"Compute the concentration gradient across the simulation box as a function "
"of the concentration difference between left and right controlled volumes."
msgstr ""
"左右の Control Volumes の濃度差の関数として、Simulation Box を横切る Concentration Gradient "
"を計算する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:321
msgid "In the folder `data`:"
msgstr "`data` フォルダ内のファイル："

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:323
msgid "`LJ_diffusion.gro`: reference conformation of 1000 LJ particles."
msgstr "`LJ_diffusion.gro`：1000個の LJ Particles の Reference Conformation。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:325
msgid ""
"`LJ_diffusion.xtc`: trajectory evolving under the effect of the stationary "
"concentration gradient."
msgstr ""
"`LJ_diffusion.xtc`：定常的な Concentration Gradient の影響下で時間発展する Trajectory。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:329
msgid "Exercise 4: Steady-state condensation process with C$\\mu$MD"
msgstr "演習4：C$\\mu$MD による Steady-state Condensation 過程"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:333
msgid ""
"The fourth exercise combines aspects of the previous three. We will use "
"CmuMD to control the driving force associated with the growth of a dense "
"phase represented by a slab at the center of a simulation box."
msgstr ""
"4つ目の演習では、前の3つの内容を組み合わせる。Simulation Box の中央に Slab として配置した高密度相の成長について、CmuMD "
"を使って Driving Force を制御する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:337
msgid ""
"Similarly to the diffusion case the plumed file that can be used to perform "
"this type of simulation reads:"
msgstr "Diffusion の場合と同様に、このシミュレーション用の PLUMED ファイルは次のようになる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:385
msgid ""
"In the folder `data`, a CmuMD trajectory ready for analysis can be found "
"together with the gromacs input files necessary to setup and run it."
msgstr ""
"`data` フォルダには、解析できる状態の CmuMD Trajectory と、その計算の設定・実行に必要な GROMACS 入力ファイルがある。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:387
msgid "`LJ_slab.gro`: reference conformation of 1000 LJ particles."
msgstr "`LJ_slab.gro`：1000個の LJ Particles の Reference Conformation。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:389
msgid ""
"`LJ_slab.xtc`: trajectory evolving under the effect of the stationary "
"concentration gradient."
msgstr "`LJ_slab.xtc`：定常的な Concentration Gradient の影響下で時間発展する Trajectory。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:391
msgid "`md_input_LJ_slab`: MD input files"
msgstr "`md_input_LJ_slab`：MD 入力ファイル"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:401
msgid ""
"Setup and run CMUMD simulations for the LJ slab system at varying CR "
"concentrations."
msgstr "LJ Slab 系について、CR の濃度を変えながら CMUMD シミュレーションを設定し、実行する。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:403
msgid ""
"Use the multicolvar-based approach discussed in Ex1 to follow the "
"condensation process."
msgstr "演習1の multicolvar に基づく方法で、Condensation の過程を追う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:405
msgid ""
"Use the graph-based approach discussed in Ex2 to follow the condensation "
"process."
msgstr "演習2の Graph に基づく方法で、Condensation の過程を追う。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:407
msgid "Monitor the density profile across the simulation box."
msgstr "Simulation Box を横切る Density Profile を監視する。"
